-- title:
--   Dimension of (X^e-1)-torsion as a sum over divisors
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be an additive commutative group carrying compatible module structures over $\mathbb{Q}[X]$ and over $\mathbb{Q}$ (compatibility being the scalar-tower condition for $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{Q}[X] \to \operatorname{End}(M)$), and assume $M$ is finite-dimensional as a $\mathbb{Q}$-vector space. Let $e$ be a natural number with $0 < e$. For a polynomial $f \in \mathbb{Q}[X]$ write $M[f] = \{m \in M : f \cdot m = 0\}$ for the $f$-torsion submodule, regarded as a $\mathbb{Q}$-vector space through the tower. The assertion is the equality of $\mathbb{Q}$-dimensions
--   $$\dim_{\mathbb{Q}} M[X^{e}-1] \;=\; \sum_{d \mid e} \dim_{\mathbb{Q}} M[\Phi_d],$$
--   where the sum runs over the finite set of (positive) divisors of $e$ and $\Phi_d =$ `cyclotomic d ℚ` is the $d$-th cyclotomic polynomial with rational coefficients. Both sides are `Module.finrank ℚ` of the respective torsion submodules of $M$, so the statement is about $\mathbb{Q}$-ranks rather than about an explicit decomposition of $M$.
--
--   This is the dimension count underlying the decomposition of a $\mathbb{Q}[X]$-module into eigen-pieces for the factorisation $X^{e}-1 = \prod_{d \mid e} \Phi_d$; it is used in the comparison of representations of cyclic groups, namely by [`Representation.exists_linearEquiv_of_finrank_invariants_eq`](thm.html#Representation.exists_linearEquiv_of_finrank_invariants_eq), where the left-hand side computes the dimension of the fixed space of the subgroup generated by the $e$-th power of a generator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Polynomial_finrank_torsionBy_X_pow_sub_one_eq_sum_finrank_torsionBy_cyclotomic.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
